@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# Record-construction coverage in dimensions 1–24
+
+Audit date: **2026-11-04**. Base: reviewed branch
+`codex/unified-discovery-reviewed-20261104`, commit
+`e25c2924f377a1061b6c60429c950d34df7515e9`. This audit adds benchmark
+recipes without modifying production operators, certificate dispatch or planner
+interfaces. It reports known reproductions, with no new SOTA claim.
+
+The [machine-readable matrix](../benchmarks/coverage_1_24_20261104.json)
+records source versions, cached-file hashes, per-dimension status flags, evidence
+paths and limitations. Coverage means a demonstrated route to the stated record
+construction. An arbitrary coordinate importer, parameterized dimension limit,
+smaller sign code or numerical candidate does not establish that route.
+
+## Source freshness
+
+The bounds below are **last recorded Cohn values, not a newly retrieved full
+table**. Dimensions 5–24 come from
+[the 2026-11-04 parsed snapshot](../../research/group_search_20261104/baselines.json),
+whose recorded original-HTML SHA256 is
+`390a3d6a5e8f2cdd3dd73a1c5c3d02fe40a4bb2373489697e697ba05c7f242c9`.
+The original HTML is not included, so this audit checks the cached JSON's hash,
+not the provenance of that recorded HTML hash. Dimensions 1–4 use the older
+[2026-10-25 cache](../../common/cohn_20261025.json), since the November snapshot
+starts at dimension 5. A fresh full-page retrieval of
+[Cohn's table](https://cohn.mit.edu/kissing-numbers/) failed on 2026-11-04
+(web HTTP 502; Python urllib HTTP 503). Search-index snippets agreed with some
+entries, but do not qualify as a fresh full-table check.
+
+Construction attribution uses the introduction and references of
+[Cohn–Li v3, dated 2026-09-01](https://arxiv.org/html/2411.04916v3),
+read on 2026-11-04, plus the sources below for superseding records. That paper's
+18D, 19D and 21D bounds are historical and must not replace the newer cached
+Cohn entries. The August `common/published.py` snapshot and some closed-package
+documentation also retain superseded 18D/19D/21D values.
+
+## Matrix
+
+`Formula / exact` means an explicitly generated known control passed the engine's
+independent verifier. `Unsupported / not tested` means no record-specific native
+generation and proof route was demonstrated in this snapshot, and no record
+reproduction was attempted in this audit. It does not mean a failed search or a
+mathematical impossibility. No target in this table was imported from an external
+coordinate file in this audit.
+
+| Dimension | Last recorded Cohn lower bound | Construction | Engine status and evidence |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| 1 | 2 | A1 | Formula / exact: `roots_a1.json` |
+| 2 | 6 | A2 | Formula / exact: `roots_a2.json`; rank 2 in ambient 3 |
+| 3 | 12 | D3, isometric to A3 | Formula / exact: `roots_d3.json` |
+| 4 | 24 | D4 | Formula / exact: `roots_d4.json` |
+| 5 | 40 | D5 | Formula / exact: `roots_d5.json` |
+| 6 | 72 | E6 | Formula / exact: `roots_e6.json`; rank 6 in ambient 8 |
+| 7 | 126 | E7 | Formula / exact: `roots_e7.json`; rank 7 in ambient 8 |
+| 8 | 240 | E8 | Formula / exact: `roots_e8.json`; 28,680 exact pairs |
+| 9 | 306 | Leech–Sloane (1971) | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 10 | 510 | Ganzhinov line systems | Formula / exact control; separate recorded numerical search discovery |
+| 11 | 604 | Bianchi–Kwon–Pappu–Zou (2026) | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 12 | 841 | Takhanov–Assylbekov–Yun (2026) | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 13 | 1,154 | Zinoviev–Ericson (1999) | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 14 | 1,932 | Ganzhinov E7 frame | Formula / exact control; autonomous discovery not demonstrated |
+| 15 | 2,564 | Leech–Sloane (1971) | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 16 | 4,320 | Barnes–Wall (1959) | Record unsupported / not tested; exact 256-point sign control only |
+| 17 | 5,730 | Cohn–Li sign modification | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 18 | 8,358 | Repository bent hexagon; K. Li tie | Unsupported in engine / not tested; separate repository package exists |
+| 19 | 12,460 | K. Li odd-sign extension | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 20 | 19,448 | Cohn–Li sign modification | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 21 | 31,560 | K. Li odd-sign extension | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 22 | 49,896 | Leech laminated-lattice section | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 23 | 93,150 | Leech laminated-lattice section | Unsupported / not tested |
+| 24 | 196,560 | Leech lattice minimal shell | Unsupported / not tested |
+
+The root recipes are in [recipes](../recipes/). The 10D and 14D recipes are
+`ganzhinov10.json` and `ganzhinov14.json`. Both dedicated exact controls were
+rerun here; the [control summary](../benchmarks/coverage_controls_20261104.json)
+records their source fingerprints and facts. The 10D `discover10.json` result is
+an earlier **numerical** search recorded in
+[validation.json](../benchmarks/validation.json); it was not rerun in this audit.
+Its separate exact known-result control does not retroactively certify that
+numerical output or its discovery process.
+
+The [18D package](../../verifications/improved/dim18-bent-hexagon/) belongs to
+the separate repository record pipeline and has no adapter in this reviewed
+discovery snapshot. For 19D and 21D, the
+[pinned K. Li README](https://github.com/Felpix-Studios/kissing-number/blob/b823640f4e98134b9d55b27288132ee954a8affa/README.md)
+was read afresh on 2026-11-04; it describes the odd-sign extensions. The exact
+12,460 and 31,560 counts come from the cached
+[2026-10-24 source review](../../common/cohn_20261024.json), pinned to that same
+revision. This audit does not replay those external certificates. The earlier
+`Felpix-Studios/D19-D21-Kissing` README still lists 12,276 and 30,779, so it is
+not a source for the larger bounds.
+
+The 11D/12D/13D/15D/16D and 22D–24D attribution above follows the bibliographic
+references in Cohn–Li v3, not new implementations of those constructions. For
+10D and 14D, [Ganzhinov, sections 5.4–5.5](https://arxiv.org/html/2207.08266)
+(v1 dated 2022-07-17; journal publication 2025) supplies the construction source.
+Newer work in other children is outside this audit's pinned scope.
+
+## New root controls and their proof
+
+[root_controls.py](../benchmarks/root_controls.py) constructs integer recipes
+from formulas without reading record coordinates. A1 is the antipodal pair;
+A2 consists of the six signed differences of three coordinate vectors. D3–D5
+contain every vector with two nonzero entries, each independently ±1.
+
+The scaled E8 set consists of 112 vectors with two entries ±2 and 128 vectors
+with eight entries ±1 and even sign parity. All norms squared are 8. Distinct
+two-entry vectors have dot product at most 4; their dot product with a sign
+vector is at most 4; distinct even-parity sign vectors differ in at least two
+coordinates, giving dot product at most 4. Thus the kissing inequality holds.
+E7 and E6 are subsets cut by `x[6]+x[7]=0`, and additionally `x[5]+x[7]=0` for
+E6, so they inherit separation. The verifier recomputes their counts (126 and
+72) and exact ranks (7 and 6); it does not assume the section dimensions.
+
+Every recipe uses the existing `geometry.integer_code` operator. Its independent
+checker establishes distinctness, norm, every pairwise inequality and exact rank.
+The shared runner replays verification for exact terminal artifacts. This is a
+formula-generation benchmark through an importer interface, not a newly
+registered root operator or a search-discovered record. Flipping the parity of
+one E8 sign vector preserves its norm and point count but breaks separation;
+the new regression test requires rejection of that corruption.
+
+There is no native Leech construction or compressed Leech checker in this base.
+Explicitly importing 196,560 points would exceed the default 20,000-point cap
+and its **19,317,818,520 pairs** exceed the 10,000,000-pair cap. A theta-series
+count from `common/theta.py` is not proof that the engine constructed and
+certified the Leech shell. Adding a suitable compressed verifier belongs to the
+core-operator work, not this benchmark-only change.
+
+## Reproduction and measured results
+
+From the repository root, using the existing Python environment:
+
+```sh
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m discovery.benchmarks.root_controls --outdir /tmp/fresh-root-controls
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m discovery run discovery/recipes/roots_e8.json --out /tmp/fresh-e8.json
+python -m discovery verify /tmp/fresh-e8.json
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m discovery.benchmarks.run_controls --controls ganzhinov10 ganzhinov14 --outdir /tmp/fresh-known-controls
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m discovery run discovery/recipes/octacode.json --out /tmp/fresh-octacode.json
+OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python -m unittest discover -s discovery/tests -t . -v
+```
+
+Use fresh output names; the CLIs refuse to overwrite receipts. The root command
+emits both executable recipes and full replayable receipts, plus a summary with
+source hashes and budgets. The static root recipes committed here are identical
+to those generated in this audit. The
+[root summary](../benchmarks/root_controls_20261104.json) records all eight exact
+controls. E8 took about 0.09 seconds, the 10D control 0.90 seconds and 14D 1.54
+seconds on this executor; these are observations, not performance guarantees.
+
+The complete discovery suite passed: **68 tests in 27.007 seconds**, including
+the new exact-root, parity-corruption and budget tests. The existing 16D
+octacode sign recipe was also rerun and independently verified at 256 points;
+it is not the 4,320-point Barnes–Wall construction. Existing SymPy modular-factor
+sorting emits a deprecation warning but the checks pass.
+
+Freshness of the full Cohn page remains unresolved. No action was denied or
+pending, and no software was installed, remote writes made, Actions changed,
+PRs opened or branches pushed.
